      "name": {
        "name": "NAD-dependent epimerase/dehydratase",
        "short": "Epimerase_deHydtase"
      },
      "description": [
        {
          "text": "<p>This domain is found in proteins that utilise NAD as a cofactor and use nucleotide-sugar substrates for a variety of chemical reactions [[cite:PUB00000446]]. One of the best studied of these proteins is UDP-galactose 4-epimerase which catalyses the conversion of UDP-galactose to UDP-glucose during galactose metabolism [[cite:PUB00025849], [cite:PUB00024593]].</p>",
          "llm": false,
          "checked": false,
          "updated": false
        },
        {
          "text": "<p>This domain also includes ADP-L-glycero-D-manno-heptose-6-epimerase (hldD) which catalyses the interconversion between ADP-D-glycero-beta-D-manno-heptose and ADP-L-glycero-beta-D-manno-heptose via an epimerization at carbon 6 of the heptose.</p>",
          "llm": false,
          "checked": false,
          "updated": false
        }
      ],
